KPL/PCK

Excerpt of pck00011.tpc, the NAIF generic text planetary constants kernel
(Nat Bachman, NAIF, 2022 December 27), retrieved from

   https://naif.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/naif/generic_kernels/pck/pck00011.tpc

Every assignment below is copied verbatim from that kernel; only the
surrounding commentary has been dropped, so the excerpt stays small enough
to check in.  It carries the orientation and shape constants of the Sun,
the eight planets, the Moon and Pluto, plus the barycentre-level nutation
and precession angles those constants refer to.  Values follow the IAU
WGCCRE 2015 report (Archinal et al. 2018, Celest. Mech. Dyn. Astr. 130:22,
with the 2019 corrigendum, 131:61).


